<header class="resume-heading"><h1>Conor Brown</h1><p><strong>Software Engineer · C#/.NET · Architecture &amp; Modernization</strong></p><p>Oklahoma, USA · <a href="mailto:carllbrown87@gmail.com">carllbrown87@gmail.com</a> · <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/conor--brown/">LinkedIn</a> · <a href="https://github.com/conorbrown-dev">GitHub</a></p></header>
<section><h2>Professional summary</h2><p>Software engineer with 12+ years of professional .NET experience and ownership of architecture, design, and delivery across operational applications, payment services, and distributed infrastructure. Leads legacy modernization, domain-driven design adoption, and cloud migration planning, and maintains the engineering standards the team builds against. Uses C#/ASP.NET Core, SQL Server, and Azure to deliver reliable operational software and improve delivery performance. Supports a team of 10 developers through architecture reviews, design workshops, mentoring, and clear standards for validating AI-assisted code.</p></section>
<section><h2>Selected impact</h2><ul>
<li><strong>Led the migration from on-premises hosting to Azure,</strong> modernizing a legacy .NET Framework MVC application to .NET 10 and merging the legacy codebase into the modern application. The work covered Azure App Service, runtime configuration, Entra integration, Key Vault identity, parallel pipelines, staging validation, and rollback planning.</li>
<li><strong>Replaced Elasticsearch with SQL and in-memory caching,</strong> removing a dependency that caused deployment and local development issues and could not be reached from Azure without a paid cloud instance.</li>
<li>Reduced deployment time from <strong>45 minutes to 10 minutes</strong> as a result of the Azure migration.</li>
<li><strong>Introduced domain-driven design practices:</strong> led event-storming and DDD sessions to make business rules and ownership explicit, then implemented the resulting DDD/CQRS workflow and rule-builder capabilities across aggregates, APIs, persistence, UI, and end-to-end tests.</li>
<li>Established <strong>in-repository end-to-end testing</strong> in place of a separate test suite, reducing maintenance overhead and keeping tests aligned with application changes.</li>
<li>Authored <strong>CLAUDE.md conventions</strong> covering DDD, dependency boundaries, modern C#, and a reference vertical slice; reinforced standards through code reviews and workshops.</li>
<li>Reduced core test execution from 8–9 minutes to approximately <strong>21 seconds</strong> through coverage-tooling changes.</li>
<li>Built an Azure Service Bus usage-logging platform designed around a <strong>99.9% delivery SLA</strong> for company-wide billing data, and remote management infrastructure serving <strong>2,000+ servers</strong>.</li>
</ul></section>
